<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" xmlns:ap242="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#" xml:base="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#">

    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303">
        <rdfs:label>PROTYS ISO 10303 AP242 Fragment</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Local, partial ontology derived from selected AP242 concepts. Configuration_Item represents a configuration concept and Product_Definition an information view; three contextual pilot rules assign PROTYS roles only to explicitly marked records. Same IRI and source type are retained. No full STEP/EXPRESS conformance or universal class equivalence is claimed.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.0</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/core"/>
    </owl:Ontology>

    <!-- ========================================
         ISO 10303 AP242 CLASSES
         ======================================== -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition">
        <rdfs:label>Product Definition</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A view of a product version characterized for a specific life-cycle stage and application context, as defined by the product_definition entity in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition_Formation">
        <rdfs:label>Product Definition Formation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A specific version or revision of a product, as defined by the product_definition_formation entity in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Shape_Representation">
        <rdfs:label>Shape Representation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A representation of the geometric shape of a product, including 3D models and tessellated geometry, as defined by the shape_representation entity in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Configuration_Item">
        <rdfs:label>Configuration Item</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An item whose evolution is controlled by configuration management, as defined by the configuration_item entity in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <!-- ========================================
         ISO 10303 AP242 OBJECT PROPERTIES
         ======================================== -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#definesFormation">
        <rdfs:label>defines formation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a product definition to the product version (formation) it characterizes, following the formation attribute of product_definition in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition_Formation"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#hasShapeRepresentation">
        <rdfs:label>has shape representation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a product definition to the geometric representation of its shape, following the shape_definition_representation relationship in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Shape_Representation"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#managesConfigurationOf">
        <rdfs:label>manages configuration of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a configuration item to the product version whose evolution it controls, following the configuration_design association in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Configuration_Item"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition_Formation"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <!-- ========================================
         ISO 10303 AP242 DATATYPE PROPERTIES
         ======================================== -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#definitionId">
        <rdfs:label>definition id</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Identifier of a product definition, following the id attribute of product_definition in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#versionId">
        <rdfs:label>version id</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Version identifier of a product definition formation, following the id attribute of product_definition_formation in ISO 10303-242</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/iso10303#Product_Definition_Formation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/research#PilotProductRecord"><rdfs:comment>Explicit selection marker of the local operational pilot; no universal identity or subclass mapping from AP242 information concepts to physical products/components.</rdfs:comment></owl:Class><owl:Class rdf:about="http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/research#PilotComponentRecord"><rdfs:comment>Explicit selection marker of the local operational pilot; no universal identity or subclass mapping from AP242 information concepts to physical products/components.</rdfs:comment></owl:Class></rdf:RDF>
